Now he's 20 behind Al Dhaheri and 36 behind Wheldon.

57:45.560 --> 57:50.760
If he really locks in, I really do think he could join in in that title fight

57:50.760 --> 57:52.680
because he's on 85 points at the moment.

57:53.320 --> 57:57.640
I've really enjoyed watching Wheldon and I feel like we should sort out his sprint races.

57:57.640 --> 58:03.800
Because in both sprint races, he's finished like 19th and 20th.

58:03.800 --> 58:08.360
Spa 1 got cancelled, of course, but in the future races, he's been so good.

58:08.440 --> 58:11.880
And he's always been able to, I mean, Spa was a bit of an off-weekend,

58:11.880 --> 58:15.240
but I mean, we saw Zandvoort was amazing from him.

58:16.600 --> 58:17.240
Double win.

58:17.240 --> 58:18.920
I think it's really funny,

58:19.560 --> 58:22.920
like the weekends that all of the championship contenders had or like

58:22.920 --> 58:25.320
most people at the top of the championship had.

58:25.320 --> 58:29.960
Because if you saw the Instagram post from FREC, it was like,

58:29.960 --> 58:31.480
‘Who impressed you the most this weekend?’

58:31.480 --> 58:38.120
And it was like, guy who finished P2 DNF P1, guy who finished on the podium twice and DNF.

58:38.360 --> 58:39.960
Or like P20 or something like that.

58:39.960 --> 58:44.920
Guy who finished P1, P5, and DNF.

58:46.120 --> 58:48.440
All of them had one bad race each.

58:48.440 --> 58:49.320
It was really funny.

58:49.960 --> 58:53.960
There's only one driver who finished in the points in all three races.

58:53.960 --> 58:55.000
Do you want to guess who it is?

58:56.120 --> 58:57.880
I know it because I saw the list.

58:57.880 --> 58:58.680
Yeah, Gomez.

58:59.320 --> 59:00.920
Oh, but Gomez?

59:01.560 --> 59:02.360
Yeah, Gomez.

59:02.360 --> 59:03.000
Hanna also.

59:04.200 --> 59:07.160
Oh, Hanna had a hell of a weekend.

59:08.440 --> 59:09.880
Oh yeah, I forgot about him.

59:11.480 --> 59:13.960
Just completely fake news.

59:13.960 --> 59:14.440
Thank you.

59:15.160 --> 59:17.880
Fake news being spread on the Grand Prixquel podcast.

59:18.440 --> 59:21.080
Hanna had actually a really good weekend because.

59:21.080 --> 59:23.960
Get P3, P2, and P8.

59:23.960 --> 59:24.360
Like that's really funny.

59:24.360 --> 59:26.840
He's actually been struggling a bit before I feel like,

59:26.840 --> 59:29.800
but he finally had a solid qualifying.

59:29.800 --> 59:33.800
And I mean, I mean, Wheldon was stuck for so long behind him.

59:33.800 --> 59:40.040
So what I think is most interesting about the standings right now is that we have

59:40.040 --> 59:43.880
generally three teams fighting for the win.

59:43.880 --> 59:47.720
And I'm glad because what I said at the beginning of the year is right.

59:48.440 --> 59:53.960
MP is a really strong team and especially around tracks like Monza that they know very well.

59:54.600 --> 59:58.840
I think they're very clearly a real threat and real team that can,

59:59.800 --> 01:00:01.640
you know, compete for the title.

01:00:01.640 --> 01:00:11.800
And there's reason why they are in P2 in the team's standings and only like 10 points behind R-ace.

01:00:13.240 --> 01:00:16.520
I think it's really interesting how our ace just like,

01:00:16.520 --> 01:00:19.640
because we had a really bad weekend with,

01:00:19.640 --> 01:00:23.400
or like a couple of really bad weekends with Olivieri and Sano.

01:00:23.400 --> 01:00:26.040
It was just Al Dhaheri that was scoring points.

01:00:26.040 --> 01:00:27.640
But then we've locked in.

01:00:28.360 --> 01:00:30.120
All our drivers are scoring points now.

01:00:30.120 --> 01:00:30.920
We're all scoring-

01:00:32.200 --> 01:00:33.160
Am I a part of it?

01:00:33.160 --> 01:00:33.880
They're all scoring.

01:00:35.560 --> 01:00:36.760
Yeah, I'm one of the drivers.

01:00:37.480 --> 01:00:39.000
They're all scoring podiums now.

01:00:40.120 --> 01:00:44.760
And we've really locked in P1 in the team's standings now.

01:00:45.800 --> 01:00:49.640
And I really just hope they can keep up the pace, really.

01:00:50.520 --> 01:00:51.080
I love you.

01:00:51.080 --> 01:00:53.320
But like, we're not locked in.

01:00:53.320 --> 01:00:59.000
We haven't won this yet because I think it's very telling that the beast,

01:00:59.560 --> 01:01:03.800
the beast like rival to R-ace will definitely be MP with

01:01:03.800 --> 01:01:07.400
Wheldon who's clearly ready to win the championship.

01:01:08.040 --> 01:01:15.800
But also the fact that Abkhazava and Chi can also definitely score some good points.

01:01:18.040 --> 01:01:24.600
What I think is really interesting is that I feel like for the first time in quite a few seasons,

01:01:24.600 --> 01:01:31.320
we genuinely have a title fight where I'm genuinely, I'm unsure who's going to win this

01:01:31.320 --> 01:01:36.760
because I know everyone said it would be Kean Nakamura-Berta, but I think

01:01:38.360 --> 01:01:43.320
it's not even delusional to say that Sebastian Wheldon is definitely on his level.

01:01:43.960 --> 01:01:50.440
And if things fall right, Rashid Al Dhaheri is more of what we've seen before where we have a driver

01:01:50.440 --> 01:01:56.600
but win it but like no one kind of really expects it and it's more of an oh, you know, maybe.

01:01:57.240 --> 01:02:03.560
But I think we generally have at least three drivers who are in contention here.

01:02:03.560 --> 01:02:10.120
And I think it's compared to like seasons with Slater and Antonelli, I think

01:02:11.240 --> 01:02:14.760
none of them are as clear off the rest of the grid as they were.

01:02:15.720 --> 01:02:22.760
I think depending on how the next couple weekends go, we really could see two R-ace drivers in the

01:02:22.760 --> 01:02:30.040
title fight and I think that would be really cool. Maybe that's just my bias. Maybe it is definitely

01:02:30.040 --> 01:02:35.320
just my bias, but I think it would be really cool to see Oliveri and Al Dhaheri both compete for the

01:02:35.320 --> 01:02:42.520
title alongside obviously the obvious picks of Wheldon and KNB. And I really do hope that Oliveri

01:02:42.520 --> 01:02:51.160
can lock in. He seemed to fix up his starts because that first weekend he stalled on all

01:02:51.160 --> 01:02:59.800
three starts, so he's really locked in on that now. And yeah, if he has another good weekend like he

01:02:59.800 --> 01:03:07.480
did this time, who's to say we don't see him in the title fight as well? I mean, yeah, I technically

01:03:07.480 --> 01:03:13.720
agree, but I think also if we're looking back at like the last few seasons or I'm looking back at

01:03:13.720 --> 01:03:21.480
specifically last season, I think he's someone that kind of reminds me of Evan Giltaire. And

01:03:21.480 --> 01:03:27.240
he knows that I absolutely love Giltaire, but he's had some real bad luck and couldn't quite

01:03:27.240 --> 01:03:35.640
keep up with the front. But then again, I don't think that either KNB nor Wheldon are on the same

01:03:35.640 --> 01:03:46.040
level as someone like Slater. So if both like the top drivers and I mean Giltaire and the same way-

01:03:47.800 --> 01:03:53.960
forgot the name- oh my god…Olivieri! you know, closer together, it could happen, but

01:03:55.320 --> 01:04:04.680
I'm on that level where I don't think we're going to see like so much surprising things,

01:04:04.680 --> 01:04:10.440
even if I would love to see it. Hope you guys enjoyed the episode. And as always,

01:04:10.440 --> 01:04:18.360
let us know your thoughts and comments. Next weekend, we're covering F2 and F3 on Red Bull

01:04:18.360 --> 01:04:26.680
Ring. And I f**king love Red Bull Ring. And if I was not called monzabanking, I would be called Red Bull Ring

01:04:26.680 --> 01:04:32.840
Lover because we saw so much great action there the last few years, especially in F2 and F3. And

01:04:32.840 --> 01:04:40.280
I think it's one of those tracks that's really, really perfect for Feeder Series because it's

01:04:40.280 --> 01:04:44.040
perfect. But I don't want to take up too much, which we're going to talk about next week.

01:04:44.680 --> 01:04:46.520
Yeah, see you guys next week.


